"mother":"Jochebed","v":[1,7,9,10,14,16,22,24,25,30]},{"id":"joshua_1727","name":"Joshua","also":"Jehoshua, Oshea, Jesus, Jeshua, Hoshea","summary":"Jehovah is his help, or Jehovah the Saviour. The son of Nun, of the tribe of Ephraim, the successor of Moses as the leader of Israel.","verses":189,"father":"Nun","mother":"","v":[3,7,14,23]},{"id":"sihon_2739","name":"Sihon","also":"","summary":"Striking down. The whole country on the east of Jordan, from the Arnon to the Jabbok, was possessed by the Amorites, whose king, Sihon, refused to permit the Israelites to pass through his territory, and put his army in array against them.","verses":34,"father":"","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"og_2238","name":"Og","also":"","summary":"Gigantic, the king of Bashan, who was defeated by Moses in a pitched battle at Edrei, and was slain along with his sons (Deut. 1:4), and whose kingdom was given to the tribes of Reuben and Gad and half the tribe of Manasseh (Num. 21:32-35; Deut. 3:1-13).","verses":22,"father":"","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"levi_1820","name":"Levi","also":"","summary":"The third son of Jacob by Leah. The origin of the name is found in Leah’s words (Gen. 29:34), “This time will my husband be joined [Heb. yillaveh] unto me.”","verses":64,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[9]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[19,22,23]},{"id":"nun_2214","name":"Nun","also":"Non","summary":"Beyond the fact that he was the father of Joshua nothing more is known of him (Ex. 33:11).","verses":30,"father":"Elishama","mother":"","v":[23]}],"places":[{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these